hadiths[2]{hadithnumber,text}:
"15504","Waki narrated to us: Zakariyya ibn Ishaq narrated to us, from Amr ibn Abi Sufyan, he heard it from Muslim ibn Thafinah, he said: Ibn Alqamah appointed my father over the headmanship of his people and ordered him to collect their sadaqah, he said: So my father sent me among a party to bring him their sadaqah, he said: So I went out until I came to a very old shaykh called Sir, and I said: My father sent me to you so that you pay the sadaqah of your sheep, he said: O son of my brother, in what manner do you take? I said: We select, to the point that we even measure the udders of the sheep, he said: Son of my brother, I shall narrate to you that I was in a mountain pass among these passes with sheep of mine at the time of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when two men came to me upon a camel and said: We are the two messengers of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to you, that you pay the sadaqah of your sheep, I said: What is due from me for them? They said: A sheep, so I set out to a sheep whose place I knew, full with pure milk and fat, and I brought it out to them, and they said: This is the Shafi al-Hail, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade us to take a Shafi, I said: Then what thing? They said: A young she-goat, a Jadhah or a Thaniyyah, he said: So I set out to a young she-goat, a Mutat, he said: And al-Mutat is one that has not yet given birth to offspring though its time of birth has come, and I brought it out to them, and they said: Hand it to us, so I handed it to them, and they placed it with them upon their camel, then they left. Abdullah said: I heard my father saying: Thus Waki said it: Muslim ibn Thafinah, miscorrected, and Rawh said: Ibn Shubah, and it is the correct one, and my father said, and Bishr ibn al-Sari said: There is no god but Allah, here is his son right here, meaning Muslim ibn Shubah."
"15505","Rawh narrated to us: Zakariyya ibn Ishaq narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn Abi Sufyan narrated to me, he said: Muslim ibn Shubah narrated to me that Ibn Alqamah appointed his father over the headmanship of his people, Muslim said: So he sent me to the collectors among a party of my people, he said: So I went out until I came to a shaykh called Sir in a mountain pass among the passes, and I said: My father sent me to you that you give me the sadaqah of your sheep, and he said: O son of my brother, in what manner do you take? And I said: We take the best we find, so the shaykh said: I was in a pass among these passes with sheep of mine when two men came to me riding together upon a camel and said: We are the two messengers of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he sent us to you that you give us the sadaqah of your sheep, I said: And what is it? They said: A sheep, so I set out to a sheep whose place I knew, full with pure milk, or: pure milk and fat, and I brought it out to them, and they said: This is a Shafi, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade us to take a Shafi, and al-Shafi is one in whose belly is her offspring, he said: So I said: Then what thing will you take? They said: A young she-goat, or a Jadhah or a Thaniyyah, he said: So he brought out for them a young she-goat, he said: So they said: Hand it over to us, so they took hold of it and placed it with them upon their camel."
